<latex-image><![CDATA[
\begin{tikzpicture}[domain=-1.5:1.5,smooth]
  \draw (-2,0) -- (2,0);
  \draw[color=seq-red, <->] plot (\x,\x^3-\x);
\end{tikzpicture}
          ]]></latex-image>
</image>
<p>
        On the other hand, the polynomial <md>
<mrow>g(x) = x^3-5x^2+x-5 = (x-5)(x^2+1) = (x-5)(x+i)(x-i)</mrow>
</md> has one real root at <m>5</m> and a conjugate pair of complex roots <m>\pm i</m>.  Its graph looks like this:
        </p>
<image width="60%">
<shortdescription>
<!-- FILL: Brief alt-text for this TikZ figure (linear algebra context) -->
</shortdescription>
